responses.corrective_action:
Root cause: APIRouter.include_router iterates through child.routes but only checks for APIRoute instances, silently ignoring WebSocketRoute instances and failing to include them on the parent router.
Implicated source: artifact://case/buggy_impl.py
Correction: replace 'for route in child.routes:
            if isinstance(route, APIRoute):
                self.routes.append(APIRoute(prefix + route.path, route.name))' with 'for route in child.routes:
            if isinstance(route, APIRoute):
                self.routes.append(APIRoute(prefix + route.path, route.name))
            elif isinstance(route, WebSocketRoute):
                self.routes.append(WebSocketRoute(prefix + route.path, route.name))'. Add an explicit branch in APIRouter.include_router for WebSocketRoute instances so that child websocket routes are copied to the parent router with the specified prefix and route name preserved.
Regression check: check.verify instantiates child routes with both APIRoute and WebSocketRoute, calls include_router with prefix '/v1', and asserts that parent.routes contains both prefixed routes with matching names. (artifact://case/check.py).

